G3521.def:
νηστεία, -ας, ἡ
(νηστεύω), [in LXX for צוֹם ;] 
fasting, a fast; 
__(a) of voluntary abstinence from food: Matthieu 17:21 (WH, R, txt., om.), Marc 9:29 (WH, txt., R, txt., om.), Luc 2:37, Actes 14:23; of the Day of Atonement, Actes 27:9; 
__(b) of involuntary abstinence: 2 Corinthiens 6:5 11:27.†
SYN.: ἀσιτία, q.v

G3565.def:
νύμφη, -ης, ἡ 
[in LXX chiefly for כַּלָּה ;] 
__1. cl., a bride, young wife, young woman: Matthieu 25:1, WH, mg., Jean 3:29, Apocalypse 18:23 21:2, 9 22:17. 
__2. As frequently in LXX (Genèse 38:11, al., for כַּלָּה; 
__(a) bride; 
__(b) daughter-in-law) and in MGr. (νύφφη, νύφη), a daughter-in-law: Matthieu 10:35, Luc 12:53.†

G3581.def:
ξένος, -η, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for נׇכְרִי ;] 
__(a) foreign, alien: δαιμόνια, Actes 17:18; διδαχαί Hébreux 13:9; 
__(b) with genitive of thing(s), strange to, estranged from, ignorant of: Éphésiens 2:12; 
__(with) strange, unusual: 1 Pierre 4:12. 
As subst., ὁ ξ., 
__(a) a foreigner, stranger: Matthieu 25:35, 38 25:43-44 27:7, Actes 17:21, 3Jn.5; ξέίνοι κ. τάροικοι (opposite to συμπολῖται, οίκεῖοι), Éphésiens 2:19; ξ. καὶ παρεπίδημοι, Hébreux 11:13; 
__(b) one of the parties bound by ties of hospitality; 
__α the guest; 
__β the host (= ξενοδόκος, Hom., Ii, xv, 532) : Romains 16:23.†
